# Table default (LOCKED)

When creating a table, use the lock in `src/Products/PinoyBusinessPOS/ExItS.PinoyBusinessPOS.React/src/features/ui-standards/table-global-default.ts`.

The locked command is `ext table soft-glass header-glossy-raise footer-glossy-raise search`.

- Table intent: `standard` (`TABLE_GLOBAL_DEFAULT_INTENT`)
- Shell: Soft Glass (`TABLE_GLOBAL_DEFAULT_SHELL` = `soft-glass`) — theme primary wash via `data-shell="soft-glass"` on `ExitsTableContainer` / playground qtable
- Header: intent `standard`, appearance `glossy-raise` (`TABLE_GLOBAL_DEFAULT_HEADER_*`)
- Header chrome (LOCKED): soft bottom raise (`TABLE_GLOBAL_HEADER_RAISE_SHADOW`) plus light left/right column edges (`TABLE_GLOBAL_HEADER_COL_EDGE_*`) — not the heavy raised stack
- Footer: intent `standard`, appearance `glossy-raise` (`TABLE_GLOBAL_DEFAULT_FOOTER_*` / `table-footer-global-default.ts`) with page-size select and prev/next nav
- Search: on (`TABLE_GLOBAL_DEFAULT_SEARCH`) — Soft Glass field inside the shell; radius follows Control Shape

On `/ui-standards` → Table playground, the fixed **DEFAULT STANDARD** sample below the interactive preview is this lock. Footer pagination chrome (page size, carets, All) stays in `exits-table-footer-default.mdc`.

Use `ExitsTable` / `ExitsResponsiveDataView` with Soft Glass shell, glossy-raise header and footer chrome, and a search field unless the user names a different recipe. Keep Soft Glass + glossy-raise CSS in `globals.css` (ExitsTable) and `ui-standards.css` (qtable playground) aligned with the lock tokens.

Change this lock only when the user asks. Update `table-global-default.ts`, `table-global-default.test.ts`, `table-footer-global-default.ts` (appearance), and the Soft Glass / glossy-raise CSS together.
